Verse 1:
[C]Once [C7/Bb]in [Dm/A]royal [F]David’s c ity
[Dm/A]Stood [F]alowly [C7/Bb]cattle shed,
[C]Where [C7/Bb]amother [F]laid her [Edim]Baby
[F/A]In amanger [C7/Bb]for His bed;
[C7]Mary [Am]was that mother [C7]mild,
[C7]Jesus Christ her [Am]little [C7/G]Child.

Verse 2:
[C]He [C7/Bb]came [Dm/A]down [F]to earth from heaven,
[Dm/A]Who [F]is God and [C7/Bb]Lord of all,
[C]And [C7/Bb]His [Dm/A]shelter [F]was a [Edim]stable,
[F/A]And His cradle [C7/Bb]was a stall;
[C7]With the [Am]poor, and mean, and [Gm/D]lowly,
[C7]Lived on earth our [Am]Savior [C7/Bb]holy.

Verse 3:
[C]And [C7/Bb]through [Dm/A]all [F]His wondrous childhood
[Dm/A]He [F]would honor [C7/Bb]and obey,
[C]Love [C7/Bb]and [Dm/A]watch [F]the lowly [Edim]mother
